5417] [17592186566143 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566143 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566143 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566143 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "57f9cf12-8dfb-53b1-b292-86ced016edb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566148 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6aa326de-d714-5b39-9140-e8acb0109c83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566190 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8792aef-971c-524f-813b-450f77f5e710" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566194 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fea3a60f-daf8-541c-b5ca-7c7fb29e64dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-3,-1]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-3,-2,-1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "003282d8-d3cb-54da-a9af-399e3a75da3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566197 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/10/10eca85fc2ab60ea0b1ee229b0a0e20110f88c4724088c0f0630d22150a8a08d.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-4x-2y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ea/eaa3ed265eac5a53eedc07f07e2ff386505a6ea5cc4934653d587e84238b540d.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c3/c332690fba1843ee09bd1466f1c978c41aff8438bf9b2a23a847ca58e2f9c228.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(-3,1)=20 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(-2,1)=16 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(-3,2)=18 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(-2,2)=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =20+16+18+14 \\\\  & =68.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a4/a4ab905de5bed2182757fa11a1945bbffec175b314918b3581d2ae062d64cdcc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1acef96d-8256-5e1a-85ce-bb35520d6331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566208 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=15.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =15\\cdot {M}_{11}+15\\cdot {M}_{21}+15\\cdot {M}_{31} \\\\  & =15({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,5]\\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50cce965-116a-5091-8060-d4b135e273bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566226 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/5b/5bd8200cb0f0aa8ca38548ae731acb54d7118e3ca735ebd5e4aebe5b6a7aa1b5.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{M}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/cc/cc616280fc457f14441e30a9e551eacf73bd56de02e68ced200302cbb1db68ac.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/e2/e2e1ab24e5d73cfc6414d7e01cd2d2d923f0f73bca137e65c9968b9142360389.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(1,0)=9 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(2,0)=8 \\\\ {M}_{31} & =f(3,0)=7 \\\\ {M}_{41} & =f(4,0)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =9+8+7+6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123056" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6d/6dcc08ca41977f189d4e873be6c060b3d8f446fb3ba2e4b0ee2667403ebb07fc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b6196d0-946b-5675-b1cf-30fba169b2db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566237 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{M}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{31})=\\text{Area}({R}_{41})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =2\\cdot {M}_{11}+2\\cdot {M}_{21}+2\\cdot {M}_{31}+2\\cdot {M}_{41} \\\\  & =2({M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{31}+{M}_{41}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/dd/dd73cb7785de514503cba6a04931a88084172b58826efdf22ea847f256c375fb.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7b6e192-3a06-52fc-8d5f-7a6810288b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566258 #edb/ref 1074 "To calculate the upper Riemann sum $U$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $2$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ denotes the maximum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nU={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =4\\cdot {M}_{11}+4\\cdot {M}_{12} \\\\  & =4({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[0,5]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,5\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3,5\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0e69171-a8d5-534f-acb8-6c56c972aa07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566266 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/77/77fdf238fb2b4046da6ddc69024378a56e4de5f46de301d5fac094cbc290b23b.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=10$ for both subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10\\cdot {M}_{11}+10\\cdot {M}_{12} \\\\  & =10({M}_{11}+{M}_{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/62/62871cd2fcc4993e0775fb7bdf0609d7849a1aa2ea5a314bc727967df590d6e7.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/9b/9b814374a5b132560656d6fe2dc2350cb693847733a40c0d21b9a13be30025e1.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(0,1)=97 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(0,3)=73\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =10(97+73) \\\\  & =1\\,700.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75184" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4fe7c63-ddd1-59b8-9a3b-8f1a0e46d1f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566267 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/6f/6fc1abc4b93b59eda024e126f8503b23f067bd9ea086a0256fcd3e67dfd7200a.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/7d/7dbec95d53ae55a09ab0a941c69f506f11be6e645a03aca3095bede1b3e966f8.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/5e/5edcabe01ac87d115a69a8b842c537187b1f1d2a003664e5fb68f7e70db3ae3d.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(2,2)=17 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(3,2)=27 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(2,3)=22 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(3,3)=32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =17+27+22+32 \\\\  & =98.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{-1,0,1\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f88ad5cd-8533-5739-b1c9-9a040c2e3b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566274 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/0c/0c68391a7a23867f21ee851aa86d389ff4dc186c3aaedde0ccb1fe15b5b4ee5b.png)\n\nThe upper sum $U(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{M}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{M}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{M}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *maximum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *upper* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $U(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={M}_{11}+{M}_{21}+{M}_{12}+{M}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+2$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/14/144142b823e7db82eb9b65e6ddc835d75a7fd8d218eab17f9db9019c4b8ab109.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a2/a2c948117d63fdd60d16ac29b3900238f7c246201bd45df3e3ee940aac0d4ee6.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & =f(0,0)=2 \\\\ {M}_{21} & =f(1,0)=3 \\\\ {M}_{12} & =f(0,1)=3 \\\\ {M}_{22} & =f(1,1)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & =2+3+3+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
